### Payment Endpoint - manual test requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains
### built-in HTTP client. Open this file and click "Send Request" above
### each block, top to bottom.
###
### Before running: start the app (`python run.py`) and seed demo data:
###   python scripts/seed_dev_data.py
### which creates:
###   user_id=1 (working card)   -> cart_id=1  ($20.00)
###   user_id=2 (card declines)  -> cart_id=2  ($10.00)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@workingUserId = 1
@workingCartId = 1
@decliningUserId = 2
@decliningCartId = 2
@idempotencyKey = 3f8e2b7a-9c1d-4e2a-8b3f-1a2b3c4d5e6f


### 1. Successful payment (200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{workingCartId}}/pay
X-User-Id: {{workingUserId}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}


### 2. Replay the exact same request (same Idempotency-Key) -> same
###    result is returned, the card is NOT charged again (still 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{workingCartId}}/pay
X-User-Id: {{workingUserId}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}


### 3. Pay for the same cart again WITHOUT the idempotency key
###    -> cart is already paid -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{workingCartId}}/pay
X-User-Id: {{workingUserId}}


### 4. Missing X-User-Id header -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{workingCartId}}/pay


### 5. Cart does not exist -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/999999/pay
X-User-Id: {{workingUserId}}


### 6. Cart belongs to a different user -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{workingCartId}}/pay
X-User-Id: {{decliningUserId}}


### 7. Payment provider declines the card -> 402 (cart stays open)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{decliningCartId}}/pay
X-User-Id: {{decliningUserId}}


### 8. Retry after the decline (run request 7 again) -> still 402 until
###    the saved payment method is updated to a working token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carts/{{decliningCartId}}/pay
X-User-Id: {{decliningUserId}}
